       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the maximum labeled adult dose of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient would be at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity. Your note says kidney and liver function are normal and there are no allergies, so nothing in the patient details explains a dose that high.\n\nCould this be a typo? Here are some common doses:\n- **50 mg once daily** is the usual starting dose for depression, and 25 mg is the usual starting dose for panic disorder, PTSD, or social anxiety.\n- **100 mg or 200 mg once daily** is typical for titrated maintenance, and 200 mg is the maximum.\n\nIf you do want 600 mg, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note on the order so pharmacy and nursing know it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
